        The bug occurs because the `__sgt_iter` function assumes that the scatter-gather list has at least one element. However, during the construction of the list, if the allocation of the first page fails, the first element is marked as the terminator, leading to unexpected behavior when the code attempts to iterate over an empty list. This results in dereferencing an invalid pointer and can cause crashes or undefined behavior.

